---
import Brand from "../components/Brand.astro";
import Link from "../components/Link.astro";
import Pulse from "../components/Pulse.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About — Alejandro Martínez"
  description="Software engineer based in Valencia. Building production systems across AI, Bitcoin infrastructure, DeFi protocols, and full-stack SaaS since 2019."
>
  <div class="page">

    <!-- ── TOP BAR ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <header class="topbar">
      <Brand />
      <nav class="nav">
        <Link href="/">home</Link>
        <Link href="/projects">projects</Link>
        <Link href="/oss">oss</Link>
        <Link href="/cv">cv</Link>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- ── HERO ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-tag">ABOUT</div>
      <h1 class="hero-h1">Software engineer based in Valencia, building production systems since 2019.</h1>

      <div class="status-row">
        <span class="status-inner">
          <Pulse color="var(--accent)" />
          <span class="status-text">available now</span>
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="bio">
        <p>
          I build full-stack systems across a wide technical range: Bitcoin indexers, AI workspaces, government custody platforms, DeFi protocols, and B2B SaaS. Most of my work happens at the system level: schema design, microservice architecture, data pipelines, protocol engineering.
        </p>
        <p>
          I prefer self-hosted over managed when the tradeoff is worth it, OSS when sharing costs nothing and benefits others, and depth over breadth. I've been the sole engineer behind Satstream and Trilo, shipped civic infrastructure at Ley Abierta, and owned two critical modules at a platform that handles law enforcement seizures across the EU and North America.
        </p>
        <p>
          Currently: building Trilo (multi-platform AI workspace), running Satstream (Bitcoin data API), and taking select freelance work through Konar Technologies. Based in Valencia, remote-friendly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── EXPERIENCE ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="exp-section">
      <div class="exp-header">EXPERIENCE</div>

      <div class="timeline-item reveal-item"">

        <div class="timeline-item reveal-item"-row">
          <div class="tl-dates">2025 — now</div>
          <div class="tl-role">Sole architect</div>
          <div class="tl-company">Trilo / Hexmount</div>
          <div class="tl-what">
            Designing and shipping Trilo: an AI workspace with autonomous coworkers as teammates, a queryable knowledge graph, and a custom DAG workflow orchestrator. Web (Next.js), backend (Bun + Elysia), mobile (Expo RN), desktop (Tauri 2) and a Python LiveKit voice agent. Live at trilo.chat.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline-item reveal-item"-row">
          <div class="tl-dates">2024 — now</div>
          <div class="tl-role">Sole engineer</div>
          <div class="tl-company">Satstream</div>
          <div class="tl-what">
            Building and operating Bitcoin's data layer. 9 repos, 4 indexers (Rust/Go/Python), 5-language SDK suite (OpenAPI-generated), MCP server, block explorer, AWS CDK infra. Indexes the full Bitcoin chain (~3 TB) for sub-second queries.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline-item reveal-item"-row">
          <div class="tl-dates">2026</div>
          <div class="tl-role">Sole engineer</div>
          <div class="tl-company">Ley Abierta</div>
          <div class="tl-what">
            190 years of Spanish legislation as Git. Hybrid BM25 + RAG retrieval with a custom int8 SIMD C kernel: Recall@5 from 2% to 66% on real citizen queries, median latency from ~120s to sub-second. Live at leyabierta.es.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline-item reveal-item"-row">
          <div class="tl-dates">2022 — 2024</div>
          <div class="tl-role">Software engineer</div>
          <div class="tl-company">Asset Reality</div>
          <div class="tl-what">
            19 months at a government-grade crypto custody platform. Owned the multi-sig governance/escrow engine (configurable approval groups, mandatory approvers, WebSocket events, Fireblocks webhooks) and the 12-chain blockchain ingestion platform (ETH, BTC, Solana, Tron, XRP, Polygon, Arbitrum, others) wired via RabbitMQ. Also: Fireblocks vault integration, platform containerization (15+ microservices), custody UI. Platform AUM grew from $200–300M to $500M during my tenure ($1B+ now post-tenure). Stack: Go, TypeScript/React, MongoDB, Postgres, RabbitMQ, AWS, Terraform.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline-item reveal-item"-row">
          <div class="tl-dates">2021 — now</div>
          <div class="tl-role">Sole engineer</div>
          <div class="tl-company">Tecpar (via Konar Technologies)</div>
          <div class="tl-what">
            Sole engineer behind Tecpar S.L.'s full platform, a B2B SaaS that operates a real electronics repair workshop (tecpar.es). Built the internal admin for technicians, the client portal, the online shop, and the public site; the system handles the entire order lifecycle. Also publishing OSS under Konar Technologies (Lovely-Logs, DiffSheets) and taking select freelance engineering work.
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── PRINCIPLES ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="principles-section">
      <div class="principles-header">PRINCIPLES</div>

      <div class="principles-grid">
        <div class="principle">
          <div class="principle-label">SHIPPING OVER PERFORMING</div>
          <p class="principle-body">A working system in production beats a perfect one in a PR. I optimise for shipping the right thing the right way: delivery first, with correctness as a hard floor. The interesting engineering problems don't appear in planning. They show up when the thing is running.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          <div class="principle-label">SOVEREIGNTY OVER CONVENIENCE</div>
          <p class="principle-body">I self-host where it matters: Traefik over Vercel for a real business, ScyllaDB instead of a managed service when write throughput demands it, Qwen on own hardware when the data shouldn't leave. Engineering-driven, not ideological.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          <div class="principle-label">HONEST NUMBERS</div>
          <p class="principle-body">CompoundFox publishes its live performance on a public dashboard. Asset Reality AUM figures come with caveats about platform vs personal attribution. Where I claim ownership, I can show the commits. Portfolio claims should survive a code review.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── FOOTER ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <footer class="footer">
      <span class="footer-left">alejandro martinez · @lyricalstring · oss under konar technologies</span>
      <span class="footer-links">
        <Link href="https://github.com/lyricalstring">github</Link>
        <Link href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lyricalstring/">linkedin</Link>
        <Link href="https://x.com/lyricalstring">x</Link>
        <Link href="mailto:alex@konar.es">email →</Link>
      </span>
    </footer>

  </div>

</Base>


<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 1280px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 28px 32px 56px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  /* ── TOP BAR ── */
  .topbar {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: 28px;
    color: var(--dim);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  /* ── HERO ── */
  .hero {
    padding-top: 64px;
    padding-bottom: 56px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .hero-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .hero-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 42px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  .status-row {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .status-inner {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  .bio {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .bio p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--dim);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  .bio p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* ── EXPERIENCE ── */
  .exp-section {
    margin-top: 64px;
    padding-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .exp-header {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }

  .timeline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .timeline-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 120px 160px 200px 1fr;
    gap: 0 24px;
    padding: 20px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .tl-dates {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .tl-role {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .tl-company {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  .tl-what {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--dim);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ── PRINCIPLES ── */
  .principles-section {
    margin-top: 64px;
    padding-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .principles-header {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }

  .principles-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 32px 56px;
  }

  .principle-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .principle-body {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--dim);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── FOOTER ── */
  .footer {
    margin-top: 96px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--faint);
  }

  .footer-left { color: var(--faint); }

  .footer-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 24px;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .page {
      padding-inline: 20px;
    }

    .hero-h1 {
      font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 6vw + 0.5rem, 2.5rem);
    }

    /* MAJ-1: collapse principle 3-col to single column */
    .principles-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 32px;
    }

    /* MIN-1: make label a clear heading on mobile */
    .principle-label {
      font-size: var(--text-mono-sm);
      color: var(--fg);
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    }

    /* stack timeline items */
    .timeline-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .footer {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 16px;
    }

    .footer-links {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
